   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "וַהֲרֵי הוּא לְאָבִיו וּלְאִמּוֹ וּלְכׇל קְרוֹבָיו כְּחָתָן שָׁלֵם. לְמַאי הִלְכְתָא? אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: לְעִנְיַן אֲבֵלוּת.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches: «And» if a one-day-old baby dies, «his» status in relation «to his father and to his mother and to all his relatives» is «like» that of «a full-fledged groom.» The Gemara asks: «With regard to what halakha» is this stated? «Rav Pappa said: With regard to mourning.»"
  }
